./ralph/progress.txt:402:- Repository CRUD invariants test file for a **composite-key tenant-scoped link table** with a database-managed version column (BE-0429 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/membership_repository_invariants_test.go). The BE-0427 user_repository_invariants_test.go shape is the closest template, but four substitutions are mandatory because the row has no own-id, has a (organization_id, user_id) composite primary key, and carries role_version + the memberships_set_updated_at trigger: (a) the duplicate-Insert Conflict test asserts on the PK collision (a second Insert with the same (org, user) pair) instead of the citext-UNIQUE-email collision — the schema has no UNIQUE column outside the PK that an INSERT could violate; (b) the existing membership_test.go's UpdateRole case already asserts the role_version atomic +1 increment, so the invariants file's UpdateRole test is dedicated to the timestamp dual-anchor (updated_at refreshed by the BEFORE-UPDATE trigger, created_at preserved) — do NOT duplicate the role_version increment here; (c) NO Delete-cascades-to-children test (the membership row is the SINK of two ON-DELETE-CASCADE FKs from users and organizations, not a SOURCE — cascades INTO memberships are proved in the parent table's invariants file, e.g. TestUserRepositoryDeleteCascadesToMemberships in user_repository_invariants_test.go); (d) the local rollback sentinel type MUST use a distinct name from user_repository_invariants_test.go's `errSentinel` because every *_test.go file under internal/controlplane/store/ shares the same store_test package — `membershipTxRollbackSentinel struct{}` is the canonical naming choice. The Insert-returns-row-with-timestamps test additionally asserts (a) role_version == 1 (the schema default that backs session-token revocation in BE-0020 auth), (b) Email + UserDisplayName populated from the JOINed users row (Insert returns OrganizationMember, not raw Membership — the httpapi layer renders the joined shape directly), and (c) created_at.Equal(updated_at) on the fresh row (the trigger has not fired yet). Seed pattern: seedOrg + seedUserRow first, then call repo.Insert through the repository (NOT seedMembership, which is the raw-INSERT helper for tenant-isolation tests). Forward-applicable to BE-0431/0432 (service_accounts CRUD + tenant-isolation) and BE-0433/0434 (api_keys CRUD + tenant-isolation) — both are tenant-scoped tables with their own version-tracking columns, so the rule "split the version-increment assertion (canonical CRUD test) from the timestamp-dual-anchor assertion (invariants test)" should also apply.
./ralph/progress.txt:403:- Repository CRUD invariants test file for a **tenant-scoped table whose only customer mutation is an idempotent lifecycle flip** (BE-0431 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/serviceaccount_repository_invariants_test.go). The BE-0427 user_repository_invariants_test.go and BE-0429 membership_repository_invariants_test.go shapes are the templates, but three substitutions are mandatory because service_accounts has no generic Update and no version column — only Insert + Disable (COALESCE-idempotent): (a) the trigger-dual-anchor test drives through the **lifecycle mutation** (Disable) instead of a generic Update — created_at preserved, updated_at moves forward via the BEFORE UPDATE trigger, plus the lifecycle field (disabled_at) is set and IsDisabled() flips true; (b) the idempotent-second-call semantics are NOT re-asserted here (they belong in the canonical CRUD test in serviceaccount_test.go); (c) the rollback-leaves-zero-footprint test asserts BOTH Get-is-NotFound AND CountByOrganization == 0 (the quota reader is the second observable surface a half-written row could surface through, and a future refactor that switched Insert to a SAVEPOINT or autonomous transaction would silently inflate it without ever surfacing on Get). Distinct sentinel type name (`serviceAccountTxRollbackSentinel`) to avoid the store_test package-level collision with `errSentinel` (user) and `membershipTxRollbackSentinel` (membership). Forward-applicable to BE-0433/0434 (api_keys CRUD + tenant-isolation): api_keys has an Update path (rotate / revoke / patch metadata), so the invariants file should re-introduce the full Update-trigger dual-anchor test from the user/membership template alongside the rollback + nil-Tx guards; the secret-bearing nature of api_keys means the rollback test must additionally assert that no secret_hash needle leaks into post-rollback observable state.
./ralph/progress.txt:405:- Repository tenant-isolation test file for a **tenant-scoped row with its own id, organization_id COLUMN, NO version column, NO generic Update, and NO soft-delete column** — only Insert + Disable lifecycle flip (BE-0432 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/serviceaccount_tenant_isolation_test.go). The BE-0428 user_tenant_isolation_test.go and BE-0430 membership_tenant_isolation_test.go shapes are the templates, but four substitutions are mandatory because service_accounts has its OWN id (no shared-identity column the way memberships shares user_id with the global users table) and the load-bearing cross-row failure mode is "two tenants happen to share a slug (UNIQUE (organization_id, slug) permits this by design) and a WHERE-on-slug-only or WHERE-on-id-only mutation swaps the WRONG tenant's row": (a) every byte-identical-snapshot test seeds BOTH tenants with service accounts holding the SAME slug via a `seedServiceAccountWithSlug(t, db, f, org, label, slug)` helper that overrides the factory's slug — a WHERE-on-slug mistake would resolve to whichever row the planner found first and the per-tenant id assertion would catch it (the BE-0430 "same user, distinct role/role_version tuples" framing translates here to "different ids, SAME slug"; the inverse is the only cross-row leak surface a tenant-root-with-its-own-id table exposes); (b) the Disable bystander test is the analogue of BE-0430's UpdateRole bystander — Disable is the only mutation beyond Insert, so the BE-0428 generic Update test does not apply; the trigger dual-anchor (created_at preserved + updated_at refreshed) PLUS the lifecycle field (disabled_at == nil) on the bystander row catch any WHERE-on-slug-only Disable that ever matched the wrong row; (c) the duplicate-Insert Conflict bystander test snapshots BOTH the conflicting target tenant's row AND the same-slug-different-tenant bystander row AND a post-state CountByOrganization == 1 for each (since the trigger is BEFORE-UPDATE only