APIKeyCannotCrossTenantBoundary; the cascade-on-org-delete proof lives in TestServiceAccountBelongsToOneOrganization and TestTenantHierarchyCascadeDelete) in the file's package-doc comment so a future reader does not look for a missing test (mirrors BE-0428/BE-0430's deliberate-absence note). Note on apierr.NotFound message vs Hint: NotFound("service_account", id) Newf-builds a Message containing the caller-supplied id verbatim, but never sets Hint — so the cross-tenant-vs-unknown-id indistinguishability check MUST compare Code and Hint only (Message would diverge by caller input, which is not a leak). Forward-applicable to BE-0434 (api_keys tenant-isolation: same shape with the same "two tenants share a slug-equivalent" angle — api_keys has UNIQUE (organization_id, prefix), so the shared-prefix fixture is the structural counterpart; plus a secret-bearing extension — the cross-tenant probes must additionally assert no secret_hash needle reaches any observable surface) and BE-0436 (api_key_scopes tenant-isolation).
./ralph/progress.txt:406:- Repository CRUD invariants test file for a **tenant-scoped row with its own id, organization_id COLUMN, NO version column, THREE distinct UPDATE paths (UpdateMutable / Revoke / RotateCredential), an additional UPDATE-but-not-mutation-state path (TouchLastUsed), and a secret-bearing row body (secret_hash + globally-UNIQUE prefix)** (BE-0433 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/api_key_repository_invariants_test.go). The BE-0427 user_repository_invariants_test.go, BE-0429 membership_repository_invariants_test.go, and BE-0431 serviceaccount_repository_invariants_test.go shapes are the templates, but five substitutions are mandatory because api_keys has no version column, three UPDATE paths instead of one, a separate touch-style UPDATE for the auth path, and a secret-bearing row body: (a) the trigger-dual-anchor (created_at preserved + updated_at refreshed by the BEFORE UPDATE trigger) must run ONCE PER UPDATE PATH — UpdateMutable, Revoke, RotateCredential, and TouchLastUsed each get their own dedicated dual-anchor test, so a refactor that dropped the trigger from one path but not the others trips a path-specific gate (the BE-0431 single-Disable pattern is too weak here); (b) the UpdateMutable dual-anchor test additionally pins the **mutable surface** to exactly {name, scopes} by snapshotting every non-mutable column (prefix, secret_hash, created_by, service_account_id, expires_at, revoked_at, last_used_at) as byte-identical to the baseline — UpdateMutable is the first repository method in the store package whose SET-clause is a true subset of the table's mutable columns, so the non-mutation assertion is the only structural defense against a future refactor that quietly widened the SET-clause; (c) RotateCredential gets a dedicated test that pins the **credential swap** invariant: prefix and secret_hash flip to the new values, every identity/ownership/scopes/lifecycle column stays byte-identical, the OLD prefix no longer FindByPrefix-resolves (must surface yerr.CodeNotFound — rotation is the only mutation that orphans a previous lookup key), and the NEW prefix re-binds to the SAME key id (rotation is a credential swap, not a re-mint, so audit trails and outstanding access grants keep pointing at the same id); (d) the rollback-leaves-zero-footprint test asserts the standard Get-NotFound + ListByOrganization-empty, AND adds two **secret-bearing redaction probes** specific to api_keys: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM api_keys WHERE secret_hash = $1 must return 0 AND SELECT COUNT(*) FROM api_keys WHERE prefix = $1 must return 0 — a SAVEPOINT-or-autonomous-transaction refactor that survived the outer rollback would surface here even when every per-id read reports NotFound, because the credential primitives (the secret hash an attacker would need, and the public prefix that drives the authentication lookup) are the load-bearing observables the table owes its caller; (e) typed-Internal nil-Tx guards run for ALL FIVE mutation paths (Insert / UpdateMutable / Revoke / RotateCredential / TouchLastUsed) — the pre-existing TestAPIKeyRepositoryInsertRejectsNilTx in apikey_test.go only asserts err != nil (weaker than the typed-Internal contract every other repository follows), so the typed-code test is additive, not a replacement. Distinct sentinel type name (`apiKeyTxRollbackSentinel`) to avoid the store_test package-level collision with `errSentinel` (user), `membershipTxRollbackSentinel` (membership), and `serviceAccountTxRollbackSentinel` (service account). Local `equalTimePtr(a, b *time.Time) bool` helper is the canonical way to express "lifecycle stamp untouched" concisely without dragging in a third-party deep-equality helper — both-nil OR both-non-nil-and-time.Equal. Forward-applicable to BE-0434 (api_keys tenant isolation: the cross-tenant probes must additionally assert no secret_hash needle reaches any observable surface — same secret-bearing redaction probe pattern documented above for the rollback test, but applied to