red + empty, Delete-happy + unknown + nil-tx, organization-delete-cascade, and a raw-SQL set_updated_at trigger pin (no bump_version trigger exists despite migration 0011's preamble). New helpers introduced (per-file DokployRef-suffix to avoid store_test collisions): rawDokployRefRow, loadDokployRefRowByID, countDokployRefRowsForOrg, mintDokployID, runInsertDokployRefOrFail, dokployRefTxRollbackSentinel. Reused verbatim: seedOrg/seedProject/seedEnvironment/seedService (schema_test.go), newStore (store_test.go). The byte-identical-bystander tenant-isolation gap-fill is the paired BE-0466 story. Forward-applicable to any future first-typed-repository story whose underlying table landed in an early migration and has been carried by raw-SQL schema tests since (a future idempotency_keys repository would inherit the same template, though without the bigint identity PK twist).
./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000048-20260519-010141.log:989:- Repository tenant-isolation tests for a **TABLE WHOSE *_repository.go, PRIMARY *_test.go AND *_repository_invariants_test.go ALREADY EXIST FROM A PRIOR (NON-PRD) SUBSYSTEM STORY + BE-046x INVARIANTS STORY** -- i.e. the tenant-isolation PRD story follows the same gap-fill pattern as the invariants story did (BE-0462 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/job_repository_tenant_isolation_test.go for provisioning_jobs). Five load-bearing differences from a first-story-for-table tenant-isolation vertical (BE-0458 deployments, BE-0456 quota_reservations, etc.): (a) NO migration is added -- the table was already exercised by both the subsystem story AND the BE-046x invariants story; (b) the rawXxxRow/loadXxxRowByID/countXxxRowsForOrg/mintXxxID/xxxTxRollbackSentinel helpers ALREADY EXIST in the invariants_test file in the SAME package store_test -- grep BEFORE writing and REUSE verbatim; (c) the lightweight cross-tenant smoke tests in the subsystem _test.go are kept (do NOT delete them) and this file is a GAP-FILL against the canonical *_tenant_isolation_test.go template (deployment_tenant_isolation_test.go is the closest template), adding the byte-identity bystander proofs / no-leak substring checks / per-tenant COUNT(*) invariance / cascade-tenant-scope proofs the smoke tests deliberately did not pin; (d) helpers introduced here MUST carry the per-file suffix (`Job`, `Dep`, `QR`, ...) and ARE distinct from the rawXxxRow/loadXxxRowByID family already exported by the invariants file (those are in the same package); the new ones to add are timePtrEqualXxx, fmtTimePtrXxx, strPtrEqualXxx, fmtStrPtrXxx (only if the table has nullable *string columns), assertXxxByteIdentical, twoTenantXxxFixture+seedTwoTenantXxxFixture, plus one or two opinionated `seedYyyXxx` wrappers (e.g. seedQueuedJob/seedRunningJob); (e) when the table has NO `version` column (provisioning_jobs is the canonical example, vs deployments/projects/se