r's home tenant) that every break_glass test needs. The 28-test shape this file lands: Append-row-shape (raw-SQL byte-equal + bgs_ prefix + server-side timestamps within ±2s + version=1 + RevokedAt nil), Append-respects-caller-supplied-id, Append-duplicate-id-Conflict (PRIMARY KEY), Append-StartedAt-defaults-to-now (the load-bearing server-side-fill probe), four CHECK/FK-violation Conflicts (unknown-org, blank-actor_kind, unknown-actor_kind, blank-reason), expires_at-not-after-started_at-Conflict (equal + predate sub-cases), Append-nil-Tx-Internal, Append-transaction-rollback, Append-peer-row-byte-identical, Get-reads-back, Get-unknown-NotFound, Get-cross-tenant-NotFound, Get-expired-returns-row-as-is (Active(t) observation, NOT Get filtering), List-newest-first-ordering (started_at DESC, id DESC), List-limit-clamping matrix (non-positive / negative / above-cap / in-range), List-unknown-org-empty-slice, MarkRevoked-happy-path (RETURNING byte-equal raw-SQL + version+1 via bump_version + updated_at advance via set_updated_at), MarkRevoked-already-revoked-Conflict (does not move revoked_at/revoked_by_*), MarkRevoked-unknown-NotFound, MarkRevoked-cross-tenant-NotFound (does not touch row), MarkRevoked-nil-Tx-Internal, MarkRevoked-peer-row-byte-identical, append-mostly-trigger-rejects-column-rewrites (per-column matrix), append-mostly-trigger-rejects-blank-reason (trigger's leading guard), organization-DELETE-cascade. New helpers introduced (per-file BreakGlass-suffix to avoid store_test collisions): rawBreakGlassRow, loadBreakGlassRowByID, countBreakGlassRowsForOrg, mintBreakGlassSessionID, breakGlassSessionFixture, seedBreakGlassSession, assertBreakGlassRowByteIdentical, breakGlassTxRollbackSentinel, sanitizeTestNameForBreakGlassID, AND the package-new twoOrgs helper for the two-org fixture shape. REUSED verbatim from sibling files: assertTimePtrEqual (drift_finding_repository_invariants_test.go), seedOrg (schema_test.go), newStore (store_test.go), wantErrCode (idempot