store_test already exposes QR, QP, and "" variants; collisions block compilation). Note that rawDeploymentRow has NO nullable string columns, so stringPtrEqualDep is deliberately not added (would be U1000 dead code). GOTCHA: when two tenants need to share a row "shape" in the cascade test, the suffixes MUST be per-tenant-unique because mintDeploymentID hashes `t.Name() + suffix` and the GLOBAL PRIMARY KEY on deployments(id) means two tenants cannot share an id even though every OTHER column is per-tenant unique — a naive same-suffix-for-both-tenants call trips mapWriteError's generic "a deployment with this idempotency key already exists" message which LOOKS like an idem-key conflict but is actually an id collision. Forward-applicable to any tenant-isolation story whose table carries a global PRIMARY KEY AND a per-tenant UNIQUE on a different column AND lifecycle triggers (e.g. future BE-0461 provisioning_jobs).
