./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000123-20260519-104132.log:8544:      "notes": "Quota dimension: monthly_deployments. DeploymentService.Create and DeploymentService.Rollback both reserve monthly_deployments AFTER concurrent_deployments inside the same *Tx as the in-tx Authorize, the deployment row Insert, the provisioning-job Enqueue, and the audit Append — so a rejection on either dimension rolls the entire unit of work back. The constant QuotaResourceMonthlyDeployments and its DOMAIN membership were already in place from BE-0006 (migration 0006_quota_policy_schema.up.sql) and the in-source quota_internal_test.go count-equality guard, so no new migration was needed. Two new concurrent integration tests in internal/controlplane/store/deployment_quota_monthly_deployments_concurrent_test.go: RejectsParallelOversubscription (20 goroutines × monthly_deployments=5 → 5 successes, 15 typed CodeQuotaExceeded rejections whose ExceededDetail.Resource is monthly_deployments, Limit=5, Requested=1, Reserved=5, Current=0; rejection messages do not echo idempotency_key, request_id, correlation_id, or source_ref; deployments row count and active monthly_deployments reservations both equal 5; concurrent_deployments reservations stay at 0 because no policy is seeded for that dimension; SumActiveReservations agrees with raw count; authorizer.calls = 20 proves authorize ran on every attempt; jobs.calls = 5 proves enqueue ran only on winners, pinning the authorize→quota→insert→enqueue order under contention); AppliesIndependently (exhaust serially, sixth Create rejects on monthly_deployments specifically — never another dimension — and no concurrent_deployments or services reservation is ever taken)."
./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000123-20260519-104132.log:8563:      "notes": "Quota dimension: concurrent_deployments. Call sites for Reserve(concurrent_deployments) were already in place inside DeploymentService.Create and DeploymentService.Rollback (reserved FIRST in both unit-of-work transactions, before monthly_deployments). This story added the BE-0336 focused concurrent integration tests in internal/controlplane/store/deployment_quota_concurrent_deployments_concurrent_test.go: (1) TestDeploymentServiceCreateRejectsParallelOversubscriptionForConcurrentDeploymentsQuota races 20 goroutines against a hard-enforced concurrent_deployments limit of 5, with monthly_deployments intentionally unpoliced; asserts exactly 5 successes / 15 rejections, every rejection carries CodeQuotaExceeded with ExceededDetail.Resource=concurrent_deployments and Limit=5/Requested=1/Reserved=5/Current=0, the diagnostic string leaks no idempotency_key/request_id/correlation_id/source_ref, exactly 5 deployment rows exist in the (org, service) scope, exactly 5 active concurrent_deployments reservations exist, zero monthly_deployments reservations exist (proves the unpoliced sibling never accumulates rows), SumActiveReservations agrees with the raw count, and the JobEnqueuer call count equals the success count (proving the Reserve is positioned before the Enqueue). (2) TestDeploymentServiceCreateAppliesConcurrentDeploymentsQuotaIndependentlyOfMonthlyDeployments is the negative complement: it exhausts concurrent_deployments by creating 5 deployments serially, then proves a 6th Create rejects on the concurrent_deployments dimension specifically (never disguised as monthly_deployments), and that the unpoliced monthly_deployments and unrelated services dimensions accumulate zero reservation rows. Verification: gofmt clean, go vet clean, go build clean, go test ./... PASS, go test -race ./... PASS, focused BE-0336 tests PASS (1.758s) under -race against real Postgres, full TestDeploymentService|ba