./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000016-20260518-174147.log:41659:- Repository CRUD-and-invariants tests for a **TENANT-SCOPED LIFECYCLE-BEARING table whose Insert is caller-id (no per-row id minting in the repository), whose only public state-transition surface is a single Cancel() with optimistic-concurrency disambiguation, and whose row body carries a lifecycle CHECK (terminal-status <-> finished_at) plus a bump_version trigger** (BE-0457 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/deployment_repository_invariants_test.go). Structurally distinct from BE-0455 (quota_reservations — the repository mints qres_<token> ids and has no Update/Cancel surface) in three load-bearing ways: (a) the test must mint deployment ids itself (DeploymentService.Create owns domain.NewID(domain.KindDeployment); the repo does NOT mint). A test-local mintDeploymentID(t, suffix) helper using `"dep_"+t.Name()+"_"+suffix` avoids global PK collisions across parallel cases without a shared atomic counter — every *_test.go under internal/controlplane/store/ shares one package, so t.Name() is the natural disambiguator. (b) The terminal-status-on-Insert probe leverages the deployments_finished_consistent CHECK: Insert's INSERT column list omits finished_at, so any terminal Status passed in violates the CHECK by construction (status terminal AND finished_at NULL). This is the one-line proof that this surface can only mint non-terminal rows; no separate trigger test is needed. (c) Cancel exercises THREE disambiguation legs against the SAME *Tx — nil expectedVersion + terminal row -> apierr.Conflict (no current_version attached), non-nil expectedVersion + version mismatch -> apierr.ConflictStale (current_version attached, verified via apierr.CurrentVersionOf), unknown id -> apierr.NotFound. The cross-tenant Cancel probe MUST include a byte-identity assertion on the foreign-tenant row (status unchanged, finished_at still NULL, version not bumped) — without it, a regression that scoped the UPDATE by id alone and disambiguated by organization_id would silently mutate the foreign tenant's row before failing the lookup. The 31-test shape (Insert: row-shape / status-default / non-queued-status-persists / dup-id / dup-(org,idem) / blank-id / blank-requested_by / blank-idem / unknown-source / terminal-without-finished / unknown-org / cross-tenant-service / nil-tx / rollback; GetByID: persisted-row / unknown / cross-tenant; FindByIdempotencyKey: present / missing / cross-tenant; Cancel: queued / running / matching-version / stale-version-ConflictStale / terminal-row-Conflict / unknown-NotFound / cross-tenant-NotFound-with-byte-identity / nil-tx; ListByService: reverse-chronological / empty-non-nil-slice / cross-tenant-empty) leaves the BE-0458 tenant-isolation file to add the bystander byte-identical proof + organization-delete-cascade probes. Helpers reused: seedOrg/seedProject/seedEnvironment/seedService (schema_test.go), newStore (store_test.go). New helpers introduced (unique to this file): rawDeploymentRow, loadDeploymentRowByID, countDeploymentRowsForOrg, mintDeploymentID, runInsertDeploymentOrFail, seedQueuedDeployment, seedRunningDeployment, deploymentTxRollbackSentinel.
./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000016-20260518-174147.log:41660:- Repository tenant-isolation tests for a **TENANT-SCOPED EVENT-LIKE LEDGER table whose ONLY public mutation surface is an unbounded INSERT (no UNIQUE on (organization_id, resource) — only PRIMARY KEY (id) and a composite-FK target UNIQUE (organization_id, id)), whose ONLY read aggregate is a SUM filtered by tenant + resource + status + expires_at predicates, and whose row body carries nullable timestamp/text columns** (BE-0456 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/quota_reservation_tenant_isolation_test.go). Structurally distinct from BE-0454 (quota_usage — partial UNIQUE (organization_id, resource) and the ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING / SELECT FOR UPDATE primitive) in three load-bearing ways: (a) the bystander byte-identity assertion must cover the nullable job_id and settled_at columns (rawQuotaReservationRow declares them *string/*time.Time; the per-file stringPtrEqualQR/timePtrEqualQR/fmtStringPtrQR/fmtTimePtrQR helpers MUST get a per-file QR suffix because store_test already exposes QP-suffixed variants from BE-0451 and a stringPtrEqual variant from BE-0440); (b) the same-resource-in-two-tenants positive-direction pair is INSERT-and-both-persist (no conflict at all — no UNIQUE constraint to defeat) instead of LockUsage-and-both-succeed; (c) a NEW cross-tenant probe is mandatory — global PRIMARY KEY collision across tenants must surface as typed apierr.Conflict (yerr.CodeConflict) AND leave the prior owner's row byte-identical AND insert no row for the requester; this guards against a regression that swapped the INSERT for an ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE (a copy-paste of quota_policies' upsert pattern). The 7-test shape (insert-bystander-byte-identity across active+settled peers / insert-row-count-invariant / same-resource-two-tenants-both-persist / global-PK-collision-cross-tenant-conflict with byte-identical prior-owner / SumActiveReservations-tenant-scoped (10-vs-300 chosen so a cross-tenant fold shows as 310