./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000016-20260518-174147.log:41661:- Repository CRUD invariants test file for a **TENANT-SCOPED COUNTER table whose ONLY public mutation surface is an INSERT...ON CONFLICT (organization_id, resource) DO NOTHING + SELECT...FOR UPDATE primitive (LockUsage), with NO per-row Update/Delete, NO version column, NO service_id pointer, and a database-managed used_value mutated by an EXTERNAL code path (quota.Checker, not the repository), set_updated_at trigger fires BEFORE UPDATE only** (BE-0453 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/quota_usage_repository_invariants_test.go). Structurally distinct from BE-0451 (quota_policies — INSERT...ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE upsert) in four load-bearing ways: (a) the second-call byte-identity proof must anchor updated_at TOO — ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING is not an UPDATE and the set_updated_at trigger must not fire (a regression that switched to ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE with even a no-op SET would silently bump updated_at and a missing anchor would let that slip past); (b) the peer-row proof is a SAME-TENANT-DIFFERENT-RESOURCE check (UNIQUE (organization_id, resource) isolates rows by resource within a tenant); (c) the row-already-exists-with-non-zero-value leg has no policies analog — pre-seed via raw SQL at a sentinel value (e.g. used_value=17, id=`qu_seed_<resource>`) and prove BOTH the seeded id AND the seeded used_value survive a LockUsage call (this is the ONLY way to prove the discarded INSERT's minted prefix id does not replace the row's id — a regression to ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE SET id=EXCLUDED.id would be a catastrophic data-loss path that typed reader projections would not catch); (d) the DOMAIN-violation test casts an arbitrary string to the typed Resource (e.g. `store.QuotaResource("not-a-resource")`) to bypass Go's compile-time check and exercise the DOMAIN quota_resource CHECK at the database layer — surfacing as yerr.CodeConflict through mapWriteError. The 8-new-test shape (row-shape, second-call-byte-identity, peer-row-byte-identity, persisted-used-value, unknown-org-Conflict, unknown-resource-Conflict, tx-rollback, nil-tx-Internal) leaves the pre-existing TestQuotaRepositoryLockUsageCreatesAndReturnsCounter in quota_repository_test.go alone as the load-bearing two-call-idempotency probe. Helper symbols introduced: `lockUsageOrFail`, `loadQuotaUsageRow`, `countQuotaUsageRowsForOrg`, `rawQuotaUsageRow`, `quotaUsageTxRollbackSentinel`. Reused symbols from sibling files: `seedOrg` (schema_test.go), `seedQuotaUsage` (usage_test.go), `newStore` (store_test.go) — note `seedQuotaUsage` is the ONLY way to set used_value to a non-zero value through a test fixture because the repository surface has no equivalent (LockUsage cannot increment).
./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000016-20260518-174147.log:41664:- Repository CRUD invariants for a **multi-table resource FAMILY whose physical realization is one table per scope in the Organization -> Project -> Environment -> Service hierarchy, sharing identical CHECK / FK / CASCADE / bump_version / set_updated_at invariants but with per-scope mutation surfaces** (BE-0449 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/{organization,project,environment,service}_variable_repository_invariants_test.go). A PRD note that reads "Database table: <name>" can refer to such a family (variables = 4 scope tables, quota_* = 3 ledger tables) — when the family is hierarchical, ship one *_repository_invariants_test.go per physical table rather than collapsing into a single mega-file, because per-scope mutation surfaces diverge (organization_variables uniquely exposes UpdateMutable + DeleteByKey on top of the bulk-replace surface; project / environment / service variables expose only the bulk Upsert + DeleteByXxxExceptKeys pair). Each file in the family extends the BE-0447 grant-table invariants template with three uniform substitutions: (a) the Upsert payload struct is the scope's XxxVariableUpsert (Value, IsSecret, SecretProvider, SecretKeyID, SecretCiphertext) instead of role + principal_kind; (b) a brand-new secret_columns_consistent CHECK-violation test is added (IsSecret=true with non-empty Value triggers the secret branch's `value=''` clause and surfaces as typed apierr.Conflict — exhaustively probing the OTHER drift directions is needless because the repository's nullableSecretColumns helper makes them structurally impossible from the caller side); (c) the leaf-scope variants (env / service) add a cross-tenant composite-FK test mirroring BE-0447's service-grant cross-tenant proof. Every *_test.go file under internal/controlplane/store/ shares the same store_test package, so the per-scope helpers MUST get distinct names — newOrganizationVariableID / newEnvironmentVariableID / newServiceVariableID, upsertOrganizationVariable / upsertEnvironmentVariable / upsertServiceVariable, listOrganizationVariablesOrFail / listEnvironmentVariablesOrFail / listServiceVariablesOrFail, and organizationVariableTxRollbackSentinel / projectVariableTxRollbackSentinel / environmentVariableTxRollbackSentinel / serviceVariableTxRollbackSentinel. The project-variables file is the smallest because project_variable_test.go already covers Upsert INSERT/UPDATE happy paths, cross-tenant rejection, the bulk delete surface, and the nil-Tx guards — its invariants file pins ONLY the row-shape and lifecycle invariants the existing tests do not anchor (version=1 default, byte-equal created_at == updated_at, ON CONFLICT id+created_at preservation, PK reuse -> Conflict, secret CHECK violation, ON DELETE CASCADE, Upsert tx-rollback). Forward-applicable to any future multi-table family at this hierarchy (a hypothetical KindOrganizationSetting / KindProjectSetting / KindEnvironmentSetting / KindServiceSetting feature would inherit this 4-file template structure).
./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000016-20260518-174147.log:41665:- Repository CRUD invariants test file for a **tenant-scoped LEAF-grant table whose ONLY mutation surface is an INSERT...ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE upsert PLUS a bulk DELETE-by-exclusion, with a database-managed version column, NO nullable scope pointer below the parent FK, and a composite FK to a leaf-entity parent (organization_id, service_id) -> services** (BE-0447 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/service_grant_repository_invariants_test.go). Structural reduction of the BE-0443 environment_grant_repository_invariants_test.go template: every leg that exercised a nullable *string scope pointer collapses or drops out — the round-trip pointer test is replaced by a service-account-principal-kind test (the closed-set CHECK leg still needs proving), the NULLS-FIRST ordering assertion in ListByService is gone (two-column ORDER BY principal_id, id), the empty-string-COALESCE dedup equivalence leg is gone (no COALESCE in the unique index), and the upsert/replace input struct drops the trailing *string field. The Upsert signature is six-positional `(id, organization_id, parent_id, principal_id, principal_kind, role)`; the ON CONFLICT branch keys on the three-tuple `(organization_id, parent_id, principal_id)`. The principal-kind cross-smuggling invariant MUST be preserved verbatim (re-upsert with a different caller-supplied principal_kind for the same principal_id; assert persisted kind = baseline). The duplicate-PK test must use a DIFFERENT principal_id so the ON CONFLICT branch does NOT match and the PRIMARY KEY (id) uniqueness violation is exercised instead of the upsert path. The ON DELETE CASCADE proof must delete the parent via raw SQL (the ServiceRepository.ScheduleDeletion is a SOFT delete and would NOT trigger CASCADE). The Upsert rollback proof reduces to ListByService-only because no per-id Get exists; ListByService is the only observation surface for a grant row. NEW Kind constant in domain/id.go MUST