./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000016-20260518-174147.log:41666:- Repository CRUD invariants test file for a **tenant-scoped child table whose ONLY mutation surface is an INSERT...ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE upsert PLUS a bulk DELETE-by-exclusion (no per-id Get, no per-id Delete, no traditional UPDATE), with a database-managed version column, optional nullable scoping pointers, and a composite FK to a parent (organization_id, project_id) -> projects** (BE-0439 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/project_grant_repository_invariants_test.go). Two structural divergences from BE-0435 (api_key_scope_repository_invariants_test.go) are load-bearing: (1) the Upsert ON CONFLICT branch must be tested with a DIFFERENT caller-supplied id AND a DIFFERENT caller-supplied principal_kind to prove BOTH the caller-id-is-ignored guarantee AND the cross-kind-smuggling-impossible guarantee — the principal_kind column is NOT part of the scope tuple, so an existing row stays at its current principal_kind even when the caller passes a different kind for the same principal_id; a single Role-only update test would silently pass while a regression that promoted principal_kind to a SET clause still went undetected. (2) The Upsert rollback proof reduces to ListByProject-only because the repository exposes no per-id Get for grants — ListByProject is the ONLY observation surface for a grant row, so it is the load-bearing leak channel a partial commit would surface through, and an absent Get assertion is a deliberate file boundary, not a gap. Insert duplicate-id test must use a DIFFERENT principal_id so the ON CONFLICT (org, proj, principal, env, svc) branch does NOT match and the PRIMARY KEY (id) uniqueness violation is exercised — otherwise the upsert path silently swallows the duplicate id. DeleteByProjectExceptIDs has TWO codepaths in the repository (len(keepIDs)==0 -> unconditional DELETE; len>0 -> DELETE WHERE id NOT IN (ANY $3::text[])), so BOTH must be exercised independently — the empty-keep t