./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000016-20260518-174147.log:41667:- Repository CRUD invariants test file for a **tenant-scoped table whose mutation surface spans FOUR distinct UPDATE paths (Update / UpdateDisplayName / ScheduleDeletion / Restore) PLUS Insert, with a database-managed version column AND a nullable soft-delete column (deletion_scheduled_at)** (BE-0437 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/project_repository_invariants_test.go): this is the BE-0425 organization template extended with the second-UPDATE-path projection (UpdateDisplayName must run the dual-anchor AND prove the path-specific WHERE/SET isolation — the row's slug must be untouched since the SET clause is `SET display_name = $3` only) and the BE-0431 inverse-soft-delete projection (Restore must dual-anchor AND clear deletion_scheduled_at back to NULL — the trigger fires on any UPDATE so a forgotten `SET deletion_scheduled_at = NULL` clause would still pass the version/timestamp anchors, making the "deletion_scheduled_at is nil after Restore" assertion the load-bearing one). Insert rollback proof must span ALL read surfaces the rolled-back row touches: by-id Get, by-org ListByOrganization, AND CountByOrganization (the count the quota layer reads), so a future refactor that switched Insert to a SAVEPOINT or autonomous transaction would leak the row into a quota check even though Get reports NotFound. The nil-Tx typed-Internal guard only needs to close the ONE mutation path the existing tests did not cover (here UpdateDisplayName) — duplicating Insert/Update/ScheduleDeletion/Restore guards already proved elsewhere is noise. Test fixtures compose seedOrg + projectFixture(f.Project(org, label)) + insertProject helpers from project_test.go; do not re-implement them at package scope.
./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000016-20260518-174147.log:41668:- Repository CRUD invariants test file for a **tenant-scoped grandchild table whose mutation surface is Insert + Update + ScheduleDeletion ONLY (NO UpdateDisplayName, NO Restore), with a database-managed version column, a CHECK-constrained closed-set Kind column, a nullable soft-delete column (deletion_scheduled_at), and a composite FK to a parent (organization_id, project_id) -> projects** (BE-0441 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/environment_repository_invariants_test.go): the BE-0437 project_repository_invariants_test.go template MINUS the UpdateDisplayName and Restore tests (the EnvironmentRepository exposes neither method — adding empty stubs that reference store.EnvironmentRepository.UpdateDisplayName / Restore would fail to compile), so the invariants matrix shrinks from six DB-backed tests to four (Insert dual-fields-anchor, Update dual-anchor, Update matching-If-Match positive, ScheduleDeletion dual-anchor) PLUS the Insert-rollback and Insert-nil-Tx pair. Update's preserved-identity assertion gains a Kind-preservation check (the SET clause is `SET slug = $3, display_name = $4` only, so kind is structurally untouched even though the column exists on this table) that the projects template did not need (projects has no kind column); ScheduleDeletion's preserved-identity assertion ALSO gains a Kind check for the same reason. The nil-Tx typed-Internal matrix-closer is Insert (NOT UpdateDisplayName as in projects) because environment_update_test.go and environment_delete_test.go already cover Update and ScheduleDeletion respectively — the matrix-closer convention is "fill the missing path", and the missing path is table-specific. New file-scope helpers `environmentFixture` and `insertEnvironment` mirror projectFixture/insertProject but environmentFixture MUST default Kind to store.EnvironmentKindStandard (the migration 0025 CHECK constraint requires "standard" or "preview" — empty string fails) —