ated_at + role + pointer columns across BOTH Upsert branches AND BOTH DeleteByProjectExceptIDs codepaths, indistinguishability of cross-tenant vs unknown projectID at the list path, per-tenant scope-tuple coexistence, shared-principal_id read isolation) so a future reader does not look for missing tests where the proof is intentionally elsewhere.
./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000016-20260518-174147.log:41679:- Repository CRUD invariants test file for a **composite-key tenant-scoped link table** with a database-managed version column (BE-0429 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/membership_repository_invariants_test.go). The BE-0427 user_repository_invariants_test.go shape is the closest template, but four substitutions are mandatory because the row has no own-id, has a (organization_id, user_id) composite primary key, and carries role_version + the memberships_set_updated_at trigger: (a) the duplicate-Insert Conflict test asserts on the PK collision (a second Insert with the same (org, user) pair) instead of the citext-UNIQUE-email collision — the schema has no UNIQUE column outside the PK that an INSERT could violate; (b) the existing membership_test.go's UpdateRole case already asserts the role_version atomic +1 increment, so the invariants file's UpdateRole test is dedicated to the timestamp dual-anchor (updated_at refreshed by the BEFORE-UPDATE trigger, created_at preserved) — do NOT duplicate the role_version increment here; (c) NO Delete-cascades-to-children test (the membership row is the SINK of two ON-DELETE-CASCADE FKs from users and organizations, not a SOURCE — cascades INTO memberships are proved in the parent table's invariants file, e.g. TestUserRepositoryDeleteCascadesToMemberships in user_repository_invariants_test.go); (d) the local rollback sentinel type MUST use a distinct name from user_repository_invariants_test.go's `errSentinel` because every *_test.go file under internal/controlplane/store/ shares the same store_test package — `membershipTxRollbackSentinel struct{}` is the canonical naming choice. The Insert-returns-row-with-timestamps test additionally asserts (a) role_version == 1 (the schema default that backs session-token revocation in BE-0020 auth), (b) Email + UserDisplayName populated from the JOINed users row (Insert returns OrganizationMember, not raw Membership — the http