+---
 - Production worker container artifacts use a dedicated `Dockerfile.worker` rather than overloading the API image: keep the same distroless/nonroot/no-secrets hardening, build `./cmd/yalla-worker`, copy `/out/yalla-worker` to `/usr/local/bin/yalla-worker`, keep the entrypoint on that binary, document that the worker has no HTTP listener, and pin the contract through `internal/release/container_hardening_static_test.go` plus `SECURITY.md`.
 - Container resource metering uses the same source/attribution/emission split as Traefik and storage metrics: source adapters normalize bounded windows into `ContainerMetricSample` values, `StoreContainerResolver` requires a live service-level `dokploy_refs` mapping before attribution, ambiguous or deleted services are quarantined before billing, and `ContainerUsageEmitter` writes only fully scoped billing-grade samples to append-only `usage_events`.
 - Dokploy monitoring source adapters are operational inputs, not billing oracles: call typed Dokploy client methods (`application.readAppMonitoring`, `user.getContainerMetrics`, `server.getServerMetrics`, `user.getServerMetrics`), normalize numeric leaves into `source=dokploy` samples with explicit `billing_grade`, keep query version/checksum metadata, and degrade optional unavailable monitoring sources by returning stable error-code entries while relying on Dokploy dependency metrics for telemetry. Monitoring endpoints that require node URL/token query params must pass a safe endpoint template into client logs/errors/metrics, and `dokployfake.RecordedRequest.RawQuery` must redact secret-shaped query keys.

